{"nodes": [{"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_ui_system_refresh", "label": "v3 UI System Refresh", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeps the existing violet identity but makes one deliberate aesthetic move: the console should read like the broadcast graphics and scoreboards organisers already trust (chips, badges, fixture cards) rather than an admin panel of tables."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_match_day_card", "label": "Match-day card (signature primitive)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The card leads with the organiser's actual question \u2014 a 'what's next' line (next matchup, court, time) \u2014 plus a played/total progress meter, and carries a 3px per-division hue border that doubles as wayfinding shared with the v3/04 board lanes."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_status_chips", "label": "Status chip vocabulary", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Draft / Registration open / Live / Completed / Archived is one vocabulary reused on cards, headers and fixtures; the Live pulse respects prefers-reduced-motion."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_card_grid", "label": "Grid to card grid with intent-ordered sort", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sorted Live first, then Registration open, Draft, Completed \u2014 what needs attention now surfaces first; empty states are an invitation with a concrete time estimate, not a grey placeholder."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_confirm_dialog", "label": "<ConfirmDialog> replacing window.confirm", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight components call native confirm() today; one promise-returning primitive adds a danger tone that refuses Enter-submit and a typedName mode for irreversible bulk ops, with a lint rule banning window.confirm/alert."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_tips_framework", "label": "Tips framework with central content registry", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contextual education without tooltip soup: copy lives in one config/tips.ts registry so it is reviewable in a single file and i18n-ready, with a dismissible callout variant for first-run moments."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_logo_placement_matrix", "label": "Logo placement matrix (org / club / team)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One logo per level per surface, never org+club+team side by side except the slideshow matchup slide; fallback chain is team then club then org monogram then initials avatar. PROMPT-32 found no migration was needed since teams.logo_path existed since V206."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_business_plan_scrub", "label": "Business-plan scrub with CI grep gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "business stays a hidden DB plan key for grandfathering and enterprise deals but disappears from all UI copy; a CI grep forbids the word in marketing and component copy with an allowlist for the plan-key literal in lib code."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_visibility_picker", "label": "Plain-language visibility picker (Private / Link only / Public)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Public/unlisted/private is engineer vocabulary; radio cards show each option's consequence sentence permanently rather than in a tooltip because the decision IS the consequence. Keys and noindex behaviour are unchanged, so no schema change."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_youth_consent_interstitial", "label": "Youth division consent-responsibility interstitial", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Youth divisions default to Private and the first move to Link only/Public forces the organiser to confirm guardian consent."}, {"id": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_org_accent_theming", "label": "Org accent themes public surfaces only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refresh.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The console stays violet so status chips and division hues keep a stable meaning; org accent touches only masthead and links on public surfaces, with a WCAG contrast guard falling back to violet. Dark mode is an explicit v3 non-goal."}], "edges": [{"source": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_ui_system_refresh", "target": "design_v3_03_ui_system_refresh_match_day_card", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "design/v3/03-ui-system-refr